<title>BRAZIL: Brazil may raise EU's car import quotas - paper.</title>
<headline>Brazil may raise EU's car import quotas - paper.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil may raise its car import quotas for the European Union to 12,000 cars a year from 10,000 as of August 21, said a local newspaper on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Gazeta Mercantil financial newspaper said Brazil could consider that measure or slight changes which would not alter substantially the country's automotive regime.</p>
<p>&quot;In addition to those two possibilities, I do not see how we could make any progress,&quot; Jose Alfredo Graca Lima, chief of the Brazilian delegation sent to Geneva, was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>Brazilian and European Union's officials are meeting in Geneva to discuss car import quota policy, the paper said.</p>
<p>According to Gazeta, the chief of the European delegation, Karl Falkenberg, said the discussions are not restricted to higher import quotas.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a matter of principle. We want to avoid discriminatory measures that affect trade and investment in the auto industry,&quot; he was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
</text>
